 "summary": "No. On BTC, ETH and SOL, entries while %B was below 0, or as it crossed down through 0.05 or back up through 0, did no better than random candles on 1h, 4h or daily. The result that holds up runs the other way: after %B went above 1, price kept rising more than after a random candle, so the short side did worse than random on 1h and 4h.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying the dip (%B below 0 or crossing down 0.05)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Inside the luck band on 1h, 4h and daily, as a level below 0 or as a cross down through 0.05."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying the bounce (%B crosses up 0)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Price did no better than after random candles on 1h, 4h or daily once %B climbed back inside the lower band."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting above the upper band (%B above 1)",
   "verdict": "worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on 1h and 4h. It holds without its strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the drop back inside (%B crosses down 1)",
   "verdict": "worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on 4h only, and only at 20 and 100 candles. On 1h and daily it sits inside the luck band."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, %B below 0 gave 10,151 entries in 2,536 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.01% ahead of random entries, inside a luck band of -0.11% to 0.13%. The level enters about 1.7 times as often as the cross down through 0.05, and the cross lands in the same place. On daily, %B below 0 trailed random by 2.52%, still inside the band.",
  "On BTC 1h, the cross down through 0.05 came out 0.11% ahead, right at the top of the band. That rests on 2 entries on Jun 13, 2021. Without them it is chance, and it is chance at 10, 50 and 100 candles. These crosses fire mostly in volatile candles, and in a window where price rose, price moved more after them because of when they fired. This is not a directional edge.",
  "Shorting while %B was above 1 did 0.25% worse than random after 20 candles on 1h, against a band of -0.12% to 0.13%. On 4h it did 0.82% worse, against -0.38% to 0.49%. Both hold without their strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles. On 1h that stretch ran between Aug 15 and Aug 17, 2021, and on 4h between Jan 30 and Feb 11, 2021. On 1h each coin shows it too: BTC 0.19%, ETH 0.21% and SOL 0.37% worse. Closes above the upper band marked strength that continued.",
  "On daily, the same short trailed random by 5.86%. That comes from 18 SOL entries between Jan 3 and Feb 24, 2021, and without them it is chance. The cross back down through 1 on 4h did 0.51% worse, just outside the band's -0.46%, and at 10 and 50 candles it is chance. On SOL 4h that cross rests on signals between Dec 29, 2020 and Jan 5, 2021.",
  "On ETH daily, the cross up through 0 looked 5.96% worse than random. The cause is 4 entries between Jan 21 and Feb 6, 2026. Without them it is chance, so it says nothing about the setting.",
  "For a long DCA bot, %B timing near the lower band adds nothing on these pairs, and the DCA orders and take profit do the work. Where %B carries information is above 1: a short bot that opens while price closes above the upper band has opened into moves that kept going on 1h and 4h. Use %B above 1 as a reason to hold off on short entries, or leave it out of a short bot's start condition."
 ],
